{"format":1,"kind":"pfa","id":"pfa-1983","version":"pfa-1983-e34903d2","year":1983,"season":"1983","label":"NFL (computed)","local":false,"source":{"provider":"Pro Football Archives","edition":"The 1983 NFL season, computed","compiler":"Pro Football Archives (the facts: starts, positions, box scores); the overall ours, computed from them and read off Madden NFL 2002 (maddenratings.net)","url":"https://www.profootballarchives.com/1983nfl.html","retrieved":"2026-11-09","method":"computed","rawScale":"value","conversion":"Ours, computed: no game rated this NFL season. Each player's season value (his club's credit, its points per game against the league's to the power 0.25, offence and defence apart, shared out: the offensive line by starts; quarterbacks, backs, receivers and tight ends by production, rushing and receiving yards, 0.2 a passing yard, 40 a touchdown and less 60 an interception thrown, and by starts; defenders two thirds by starts and one third by plays, 2 a sack where recorded, 1.5 an interception, 1 a fumble recovered, 1 a return touchdown; kickers by field goals, extra points and accuracy against the league) is ranked among the league-season's players at his game position (ties by starts, then games played) and read off Madden NFL 2002's overalls at that position (the 2001 season: maddenratings.net's 31 team spreadsheets, punters left out), as many of each Madden team's best as the season carries per club, by linear interpolation; rounded and held to 1–99. Then each club moves toward its results: its target is T = μ + √r × S ÷ m, where S is its Simple Rating System (its margins by least squares with a home edge, the NFL's ratings summing to nought) from the season's 224 games, r = 0.617 their reliability, m = 1.893 points of margin a game for each point of the strength the match model plays (its lineup's offence and defence, their mean), measured over 160,000 simulated games under the season's rules, and μ = 78.95 the clubs' mean strength before the move. Every player of a club moves by one whole number and its best few by one more, held to 1–99 and never past a teammate rated above him, whichever brings the club nearest its target: −3 to +3 points this season. The results count twice, by design: the credit's points for and against place a club's players at their positions and weigh its offence against its defence, and the move then sets the club's level from its margins, wherever the credit left it. Facts from Pro Football Archives; the weights tuned once on 2001–2005 against the next season's Madden launch ratings, then frozen."},"map":"nfl1982","clubs":[{"id":"nfl-washington","name":"Washington","code":"WAS","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 340)","str":84.8,"squad":[["Joe Theismann","QB",98],["Bob Holly","QB",55],["John Riggins","RB",94],["Joe Washington","RB",77],["Charlie Brown","WR",90],["Art Monk","WR",79],["Alvin Garrett","WR",71],["Virgil Seay","WR",64],["Rick Walker","TE",79],["Don Warren","TE",76],["George Starke","OL",98],["Jeff Bostic","OL",98],["Joe Jacoby","OL",98],["Russ Grimm","OL",98],["Mark May","OL",89],["Ken Huff","OL",58],["Bruce Kimball","OL",53],["Dave Butz","DL",87],["Dexter Manley","DL",87],["Darryl Grant","DL",76],["Todd Liebenstein","DL",75],["Tony McGee","DL",69],["Charles Mann","DL",63],["Mel Kaufman","LB",83],["Neal Olkewicz","LB",81],["Rich Milot","LB",77],["Vernon Dean","CB",75],["Darrell Green","CB",74],["Anthony Washington","CB",65],["Brian Carpenter","CB",59],["Mark Murphy","S",90],["Curtis Jordan","S",70],["Ken Coffey","S",66],["Mark Moseley","K",95]]},{"id":"nfl-los-angeles-raiders","name":"Los Angeles Raiders","code":"RAI","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 277)","str":82.5,"squad":[["Jim Plunkett","QB",81],["Marc Wilson","QB",71],["Marcus Allen","RB",93],["Kenny King","RB",78],["Cliff Branch","WR",81],["Malcolm Barnwell","WR",80],["Calvin Muhammad","WR",67],["Dokie Williams","WR",64],["Todd Christensen","TE",99],["Don Hasselbeck","TE",